m/users/fu7mu4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fu7mu4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fu7mu4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fu7mu4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fu7mu4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fu7mu4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-19T12:52:18Z","updated_at":"2022-07-19T12:52:18Z","body":"@jlovejoy I've never seen this license at all except that https://opensource.apple.com/source/mDNSResponder/mDNSResponder-320.10/mDNSPosix/nss_ReadMe.txt\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1189015396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1192140983","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1528#issuecomment-1192140983","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1528","id":1192140983,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85HDqC3","user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-22T03:25:48Z","updated_at":"2022-07-22T03:25:48Z","body":"# New submission review\r\n\r\n## Has the license been approved by the OSI? No\r\n\r\n## Definitive factors\r\n\r\n### Is the submitted license unique, that is, it does not match another license already on the License List as per the matching guidelines?  Unique enough – it is only a 41.8% match to the [Intel Open Source License - Intel](https://spdx.org/licenses/Intel.html).   Also note, the Intel License has been retired by OSI.  \r\n\r\n### If a software license, does it apply to source code and not only to executables?\r\n\r\nYes -  language includes “to use and deal with the Software in source code and binary forms without restriction.”\r\n\r\n### Does the license have identifiable and stable text, and is not in the midst of drafting?\r\n\r\nMost likely stable as this is a license that applies to older components and no longer seems to be in active drafting.\r\n\r\n### Has the license steward, if any, committed to versioning new versions in the future and to not modify it after addition to the list?\r\n\r\nWe could not definitely determine who the license steward was – may no longer exist.  Searching on nicta.com.au takes one to a completely different organization:  https://data61.csiro.au/.  There is an author reference to Andrew White at Nicta in this doc:   https://opensource.apple.com/source/mDNSResponder/mDNSResponder-320.10/mDNSPosix/nss_ReadMe.txt (circa 2004).  Searching this name on LinkedIn did not reveal any definitive candidates.  \r\n\r\n## Other factors for inclusion\r\n\r\n### 1. Does the license substantially comply with one of the free/open content definitions?\r\n\r\nLargely meets the Open Source Definition but for the following additional cure provisions:\r\n\r\n\r\nIf applicable legislation implies warranties or conditions, or imposes obligations or liability on NICTA in respect of the Software that cannot be wholly or partly excluded, restricted or modified, NICTA's liability is limited, to the full extent permitted by the applicable legislation, at its option, to:  \r\na. in the case of goods, any one or more of the following:  i. the replacement of the goods or the supply of equivalent goods; ii. the repair of the goods; iii. the payment of the cost of replacing the goods or of acquiring equivalent goods; iv. the payment of ther country to which the U.S. has embargoed goods and services. st of having the goods repaired; or b. in the case of services: i. the supplying of the services again; or ii. the payment of the cost of having the services supplied again.\r\n\r\n\r\n### 2. Is the license structured to be generally usable by anyone, and not specific to one organisation or project?\r\n\r\nYES.\r\n\r\n\r\n### 3. Does the license have substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered (ie. use in many projects, or in one significant project)?\r\n*For recently written licenses, definitive plans for it to be used in at least one or a few significant projects may satisfy this*\r\n\r\nAs discussed, this project that uses this old license, libnss_mdns, is used in Debian, most web browsers, been around for some time. It looks like the project has (somehow) changed the license to LGPL-2.1-or-later, but this license is still in general circulation for foundational components deep in software stacks.  See, [OpenCores](https://opencores.org/websvn/filedetails?repname=c0or1k&path=%2Fc0or1k%2Ftrunk%2Fconts%2Flibc%2Finclude%2Fstdio.h&rev=0).  \r\n\r\n### 4. Is the license primarily intended to facilitate the free distribution of content with limited restrictions?\r\n\r\nYES (also note that this license removed the Intel export restrictions). \r\n\r\n### 5. Does the license steward support this submission, or is at least aware of and not in opposition of it?\r\n\r\nNot in opposition as far as we know – unable to contact the steward.\r\n\r\n## Summary of factors / outcome\r\n\r\nRecommend that we approve this license per discussions in the July 14th meeting.  Determined to be in sufficient circulation that providing an identifier will serve the SPDX’s mission of software identification.  \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1192140983/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1198325688","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1528#issuecomment-1198325688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1528","id":1198325688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85HbP-4","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-28T15:42:05Z","updated_at":"2022-07-28T15:42:05Z","